-// Chapter 33 checkpoint 3: the closest-hit shader reports the geometry of the hit.
+// Chapter 33 checkpoint 4: the material comes from the record the traversal selected.
 //
-// `RayTCurrent()` is the parametric distance of the committed hit along the ray. Every ray in this lab has a
-// unit-length direction, so it is a distance in metres, and every surface in the scene is a plane perpendicular
-// to the ray, so the values it is allowed to take are known before the frame runs.
+// This is the mechanism the chapter exists for. The shader table's hit-group section holds four records that all
+// name the same hit group and differ only in the five 32-bit values stored after their 32-byte shader
+// identifiers. Those values are the hit group's *local* root arguments: the state object associates a local root
+// signature with the hit group and with nothing else, so the runtime binds them from the record the traversal
+// selected rather than from the command list, and two records that name the same code are two different
+// materials.
 //
-// The barycentric attributes are where inside the triangle the intersection landed. DXR hands a triangle
-// closest-hit shader a `BuiltInTriangleIntersectionAttributes` whose two floats are the pair (b1, b2) that
-// weights the vertices as v0 * (1 - b1 - b2) + v1 * b1 + v2 * b2. Only two of the three weights are stored
-// because the third is implied, which is why the attribute size the state object declares is eight bytes rather
-// than twelve.
+// The selection is D3D12's and the shader cannot influence it. The record index is the sum of four terms - the
+// ray contribution, the geometry multiplier times the geometry's index inside its bottom-level structure, and the
+// instance's own contribution - and none of them is visible to the shader that ends up running. A closest-hit
+// shader that reports the index baked into its own record therefore reports which record the traversal chose,
+// which no amount of shader arithmetic could prove on its own.
 //
-// The record the traversal selected and the colour it carries are still missing, so every hit is still black.
+// The terms the configuration owns are still fixed at the trace call, so the frame answers only the default
+// selection.

 #include "../Common/DxrShared.hlsli"

